course: dictionary
lesson: 567
title: Words for family and respect
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Aunty is a friendly, informal word. Most often it is a name for an aunt, your mother's or father's sister, or your uncle's wife. In «In London, Elodie's mum is a nurse who works nights, so on those nights Elodie stays with Aunty Roisin», Aunty is used as a name, so it starts with a capital A.
explain: Aunty can also be a respectful name for an older woman who is a family friend or an elder, even if she is not a real relative. The sentence does not say whether Aunty Roisin is a real aunt. The clues are that Elodie stays with her on nights when her mum works, and that she makes the best stew in Peckham. Read the clues before you decide.
explain: In some Aboriginal Australian and Māori communities, Aunty is a title of respect for a female elder. Auntie with a capital A is also a nickname for the BBC. So check the capital letter and the sentence around the word to be sure which meaning the writer means.
fact: Aunty is an informal word for an aunt, and it can also be spelt auntie.
fact: «Aunty» means your mother's or father's sister, or your uncle's wife.
fact: «Aunty» can be a respectful name for an older woman who is a family friend, not a real relative.
fact: In Aboriginal Australian and Māori communities, «Aunty» is a title of respect for a female elder.
fact: «Auntie», with a capital A, is a nickname for the BBC in the UK.
exercise: Which spelling is also allowed for aunty? | awnty | *auntie | antie | aunti
exercise: Which word means your mother's or father's sister? | niece | cousin | nephew | *aunty
exercise: In Aboriginal Australian and Māori communities, what does «Aunty» show? | A job in a shop | Anger at a neighbour | A holiday in a caravan | *Respect for a female elder
test: In «Elodie stays with Aunty Roisin», the capital A shows something. What does it tell you? | *It is a name, not just the word for an aunt | It shows the sentence is a question | It means she is a nurse who works nights
test: Which nickname for the BBC is written with a capital A? | Aunty | Aunt | *Auntie | Antie
exam: Maya calls her neighbour Mrs Osei, who is not a real relative, «Aunty» out of respect. What does Aunty show here? | A job in a shop | A nickname for the BBC | *Respect for an older family friend | A real family tie, like a sister
